solid lancet_tube_body_PLACEHOLDER
# SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-W-2.0
# Copyright (c) 2026 Lambert iGEM 2025 Team and contributors
#
# THIS FILE IS A PLACEHOLDER. It does not contain printable mesh data.
# The real STL will be exported from the Fusion 360 parametric source
# and committed in the v0.1.0 release tagged for Zenodo archiving.
#
# Description of the intended part (matches the dimensions claimed in
# the HardwareX paper, Section 3.1):
#
#   Part:     three-compartment cartridge body
#   Material: clear polycarbonate filament
#   Outer diameter:  ~12 mm
#   Total height:    ~30 mm
#   Compartment volume: ~200 microlitres each
#   Friction-fit tolerance: 0.1 mm at each compartment seam
#   Sealing surface: one layer of PTFE thread tape
#                    (~0.075 mm thickness) wrapped around each
#                    interior friction-fit ridge
#   Derived from: the open-source 1.5 mL laboratory tube model by
#                 Bobby Dyer (Thingiverse), modified to a three-
#                 compartment vertical stack with a press-fit cap
#                 carrying a reagent-loading port.
#
# Slicing parameters: 0.1 mm layer height, 100 % infill,
# 260 C nozzle, 105 C bed. Anneal at 80 C for 30 min after printing.
#
# To regenerate this file from the parametric source:
#   1. Open `tube_assembly.f3d` (forthcoming) in Autodesk Fusion 360.
#   2. Suppress the cap component.
#   3. Right-click the body component and choose Save As Mesh -> STL.
#   4. Use refinement "high" and units "mm". Replace this file.
endsolid lancet_tube_body_PLACEHOLDER
